  "body": "From M3's review of PR #1623 (#1560): the cross-hole (radial hole) half of `operation/hole_digest.rs`, which feeds the Drill op's stamp, is not pinned. Dropping `dir`, `radius` or `floor_d` from the digest stays green, so a changed radial hole could leave its op reading Fresh. This predates #1623; the digest only moved code.\n\nAlso: the comments in hole_digest.rs and the decision file call the lattice \"1 µm\", but `cl::lattice` is 1e-6 mm (a nanometre). Fix the wording.\n\n**Done means:** a unit pin changes each cross-hole field (dir, radius, floor_d and the rest) by one lattice step past rounding and asserts the stamp moves. Dropping any field from the digest goes red. The lattice wording is corrected.\n\nRelated: #1560, PR #1623, #1351.\n",
